{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"b11b8902-6f16-45fe-a46a-ba722a55a00c","status":"SUCCESS","response":"I have updated the workout generator in [`hr_target`](file:///tmp/h-DoTSyJ/gen.py#L10-L13) ([gen.py](file:///tmp/h-DoTSyJ/gen.py)) and documented the change and rationale in [ANSWER.md](file:///tmp/h-DoTSyJ/ANSWER.md).\n\n### Summary\n- **What changed**: Renamed the lower-bound key in `hr_target` from `\"value\"` to `\"start\"` (`{\"units\": \"%lthr\", \"start\": lo, \"end\": hi}`).\n- **Why**: In Intervals.icu's `workout_doc` schema, `{\"value\", \"end\"}` exports to Garmin FIT as a Lap-HR / zone-mapped target (which the watch clamps to its own local HR zone edges), whereas `{\"start\", \"end\"}` exports as an Instant-HR corridor with the exact BPM range calculated from Intervals.icu's LTHR.\n","duration_seconds":91.1801,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":58688,"output_tokens":1722,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":143927,"total_tokens":60410}}}
